<title>UK: UK Apr global trade deficit 961 mln stg.</title>
<headline>UK Apr global trade deficit 961 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics issued the following data on Britain's global trade in April (in million stg, previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    GLOBAL TRADE	     April	   March     (PREL Mar)</p>
<p>    Trade balance		-961	    -671	 (-671)</p>
<p>    Exports		    14,672	  13,643     (13,643)</p>
<p>    Imports		    15,633	  14,314     (14,314)</p>
<p>    EU trade balance	   -536	    -20	   (-20)</p>
<p>    EU exports		  8,054	   7,929	 (7,929)</p>
<p>    EU imports		  8,590	   7,949	 (7,949)</p>
<p>    TRADE VALUE EX OIL/ERRATICS     Apr     March  (PREL Mar)</p>
<p>    Trade balance (in million stg)	-1,478   -1,297  (-1,297)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) -0.5%   -2.5%    (-2.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports)  1.5%   UNCH     (unch)</p>
<p>TRADE VOLUME EX OIL/ERRATICS</p>
<p>    Import volume index (base 1990) 141.4   127.4    (127.4)</p>
<p>    Export volume index (base 1990) 153.2   141.5    (141.5)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (imports) 1.0%    -0.5%     (unch)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (imps) 4.5%    3.0%	(3.5%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on pvs qtr (exports) 2.5%    2.0%	(2.0%)</p>
<p>    Latest qtr on yr-ago qtr (exps) 6.5%    6.0%	(6.5%)</p>
<p>    TRADE IN OIL (VALUE MLN STG)	Apr     Mar   (PREL Apr)</p>
<p>    BALANCE				   374     604	(604)</p>
<p>    EXPORTS				   843     960	(960)</p>
<p>    IMPORTS				   469     356	(356)</p>
<p>Economists had forecast a deficit of 625 million stg.</p>
<p>The ONS said the erratic pattern of the deficit makes estimation of the trend difficult. Bearing this in mind, the latest estimate of trend, based on data to April, suggest that the whole world goods deficit is broadly flat.</p>
</text>
